Third-party software

The project's MIT License applies to Codex Trace's own code. Third-party
components retain their respective licenses and copyright notices.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and LICENSES/ in the plugin package, or third_party/
in the source repository, for the dependency inventory and full upstream texts.
The GitHub community marketplace package does not bundle Python or Python
dependency code. uv obtains and manages the pinned runtime and dependencies
in external caches. Those components retain their upstream license terms.
The portable installer ZIP does not bundle Python or Python dependency code;
it prepares a separate local environment and installs the locked dependencies.
The optional platform-specific offline plugin ZIP bundles a standalone CPython
runtime and Python dependency code. Its runtime/LICENSES/cpython-runtime/
directory contains the supplied runtime-distribution license and notice texts;
runtime/runtime-provenance.json records their hashes and distribution source.
The runtime distribution can include libraries with their own terms, so its
full license collection must accompany that package. The external Codex
executable is provided by the user's local installation and is not bundled
in any distribution.
